(Compile-fail: bug #88 - the declaration path always knew `not <text>` was a
 boolean and refused to initialise a number with one. That is the reading the
 segfault contradicted: handed the same expression, Print was told it was
 text and dereferenced the boolean 0. The type-check stays, and is the proof
 that a `not` is boolean-valued whatever its operand.)

a text called greeting is "hi".
a number called answer is not greeting.
